# Frontend Development

- Use the App Router under `app/`. Use `.jsx` for pages, layouts, loading/error/not-found files, and any file containing JSX; use `.js` for non-React utilities and helpers.
- Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only for interactivity, browser APIs, or client hooks.
- Route groups: `app/(public)`, `app/(admin)`, `app/(manager)`, `app/(waiter)`, `app/(chef)`, `app/(cashier)`, and `app/(customer)`. Keep their role names aligned with the server; route gating is UX, not authorization.
- Put shared UI in `components/`, fetch/API helpers in `lib/`, reusable client logic in `hooks/`.
- Colocate feature UI (for example `components/orders/OrderTable.jsx`) instead of one giant file.
- Keep pages thin: compose components and call lib helpers; do not embed business rules.
- Fetch on the server when possible; use client fetches for live/kitchen/interactive views.
- Implement one flow at a time. Do not scaffold every module at once.

```javascript
// app/(admin)/orders/page.jsx — server component, no 'use client'
import { OrderTable } from "../../../components/orders/OrderTable";
import { getOrders } from "../../../lib/api/orders";

export default async function OrdersPage() {
  const { data } = await getOrders();
  return <OrderTable orders={data ?? []} />;
}
```
